        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): unref detached qa cli child and detach stdio listeners",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`runQaCli` spawns a **detached** child (non-Windows) but never `unref()`s it and never removes the `stdout`/`stderr` `data` listeners on `close`. On the success path the promise resolves while the detached process and its pipe listeners stay attached, so the parent's event loop cannot exit until the child exits.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`unref()` the child after spawn so a completed qa cli run does not keep the caller alive, and remove the data listeners on `close` so the resolved stream is not retained.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA Lab suite runs and the host process can exit promptly after a qa cli invocation completes; no change to success/failure behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression test \"unrefs the detached child so it cannot keep the parent event loop alive\": asserts `child.unref()` is called once and stdio `data` listeners are detached on `close`. **Red before the fix** (`unref` called 0 times), green after.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.test.ts` → 28 passed.\n- Verified `upstream/main` is byte-identical for this region (not yet fixed), so this PR is not a duplicate.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed: `runQaCli` in `extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.ts` spawns a detached qa-cli child but never `unref()`s it and never removes the stdout/stderr `data` listeners on close, so the parent's event loop could stay alive (or retain the resolved stream) after the promise settles. The fix calls `child.unref()` and detaches both listeners in the `close` handler.\n\nReal environment tested: macOS 15, Node v24.18.0 (Homebrew node@24), vitest 4.1.9. The changed spawn/unref/listener path is driven through a mocked `node:child_process` so the exact `child.unref()` call and listener detachment are asserted without spawning real processes.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n- `npx vitest run extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.test.ts`\n\nEvidence after fix (CI `Real behavior proof` job passed; local suite asserts):\n```\n- \"unrefs the detached child so it cannot keep the parent event loop alive\" -> child.unref called exactly once\n- stdout/stderr data listeners removed on close so the resolved stream is not retained\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: The detached child is unref'd exactly once and both stream listeners are detached on `close`, so the caller can exit without reaping or retaining the child. The `Real behavior proof` CI check passed for this head.\n\nWhat was not tested: A real subprocess spawn against a live qa-cli binary was not executed (the spawn is fully mocked); the proof targets the exact changed lines — the `unref()` call and listener cleanup — which are process-control contracts, not business logic.\n",
        "branch": "fix/qa-cli-detached-child-unref",
